  "note": "Triennial election of the councillors of Londonderry Corporation, polled Wednesday 18 May 1949 (the aldermanships were not included). The Unionist nominees for the North Ward were returned unopposed on nomination day, 4 May (Derry Journal, 6 May 1949, p. 5); the Irish Labour Party contested the South and Waterside wards. Result: Anti-Partitionists 7 seats instead of 4; Unionist control retained. A.P. = Anti-Partition (the News-Letter prints N.); I.L.P. = Irish Labour Party (News-Letter: Eire Lab.). John Doherty's and Deeney's votes are the News-Letter and Irish News figures (the Journal's OCR is unclear, 887 for Deeney)."
